<p>Israel said it struck Gaza City on Friday in an operation targeting Izz al-Din al-Haddad, whom Israeli officials described as the head of Hamas’ armed wing in the Gaza Strip and one of the planners of the Oct. 7, 2023, Hamas-led attack on southern Israel. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and Defense Minister Israel Katz later said Israeli forces had killed al-Haddad. Medical sources in Gaza said Palestinians were killed and wounded in the Friday strikes, which Reuters-based accounts and Israeli media said hit a residential building in Gaza City’s Rimal neighborhood and a vehicle. Israel accused al-Haddad of holding Israeli hostages, directing attacks against Israeli forces and refusing to carry out a U.S.-led agreement under President Trump for Hamas’ disarmament and the demilitarization of Gaza. Several accounts said al-Haddad became Hamas’ military commander in Gaza after Israel killed Mohammad Sinwar in May 2025.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/xN3FBnUM4iiL7QxYQ-8TSrUcRLgaMTOGStMpimakL76NEu3KnK7ZsbeiSVTbkPLGCHaLBF3MzuRfeF71Y5SZ7KwHgFMY9DR64T7OTV26hzM7gSlrB5Ezxpb_XJ5hPuThzfMUdyMSSM7jtQayFFuykZSRdHTvRDvbQf19DepUu4N4ZbheuzYvNYHreaH-EVw7N9urFu41lIxfK3X_R_hf7h1tOjXUtd5tg_no2JnA_ku7V9HsVd9I-iBcpd9OeEd82gkUQ3A' alt='A fire burns in a residential apartment after Israeli shelling, according to the Ministry of Health, in Gaza City May 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Most-wanted status: Middle East Eye and Infobae said Israel had placed al-Haddad on its most-wanted list.</li><li>Remaining leader: Israeli reports described al-Haddad as the last Hamas official still in Gaza who had belonged to the group’s leadership before Oct. 7, 2023.</li><li>Territory claim: Netanyahu said Israel controlled 60% of Gaza, according to a Middle East Monitor item summarizing Israeli statements.</li><li>Ceasefire context: CNN-linked and Greek reports said the strike came during an ongoing ceasefire, with some outlets describing it as a breach.</li></ul><blockquote>Al-Haddad was responsible for the murder, abduction, and harm inflicted upon thousands of Israeli civilians and IDF soldiers - Office of Israeli Defense Minister Israel Katz</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli government: Netanyahu and Katz framed the strike as an assassination of a senior Hamas commander and a warning to other Hamas leaders; Greek reporting quoted their message that Israel would find such figures “sooner or later.” (<a href='https://www.tanea.gr/2026/05/15/world/netaniaxou-elegxoume-to-60-tis-loridas-tis-gazas-nekros-o-igetis-tis-xamas/'>Ta Nea</a>, <a href='https://www.protothema.gr/world/article/1819438/neo-htupima-tou-israil-sti-lorida-tis-gazas-kata-igeti-tis-hamas/'>Proto Thema</a>)</li><li>Hamas: Hamas had not issued an immediate response after Israeli officials said they had killed al-Haddad. (<a href='https://www.middleeasteye.net/live-blog/live-blog-update/israel-assassinated-hamas-military-commander-izz-al-din-al-haddad'>Middle East Eye</a>)</li><li>Gaza medical workers: Medical workers reported Palestinian deaths and injuries from the strikes, and Reuters footage cited in Danish reporting showed Palestinians pulling at least one body from the rubble of a badly damaged, burning building. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-targets-head-of-hamas-armed-wing-with-gaza-strike'>The Straits Times</a>, <a href='https://www.kristeligt-dagblad.dk/udland/meldinger-om-flere-draebte-i-israelsk-angreb-mod-hamas-leder-i-gaza'>Kristeligt Dagblad</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-targets-top-hamas-militant-leader-in-gaza-strike/article70984711.ece'>Israel says carried out Gaza strike targeting head of Hamas armed wing</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/15/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-haddad-hamas.html'>Israeli Strike Targeted Top Hamas Leader in Gaza, Officials Say</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/